Runback is commercial software with a free, source-available Community edition.
Two licences apply:

• Community edition — Runback Community Licence — see LICENSE-COMMUNITY.
  The core developer toolchain: run capture, deterministic time-travel replay,
  the signed re-executable audit record, evals + the release gate, and a single
  workspace. Free to install, run, and self-host — no licence token required.
  The source is published: you may read, modify, and redistribute it under that
  licence. This is source-available, NOT open source — the licence restricts the
  field of use (you may not offer Runback to third parties as a hosted or managed
  service), which the Open Source Definition does not permit.

• Enterprise Features — Runback Commercial Licence — see LICENSE-ENTERPRISE.
  Multi-tenant workspaces, the fleet dashboard, team roles (RBAC), SSO, alerting,
  usage metering/billing, and long retention. Production use requires a signed
  Runback licence token (RUNBACK_LICENSE). Setting an arbitrary value does not
  unlock them — the token is cryptographically verified. Their source is not
  included in the Community repository.

All rights not expressly granted are reserved. LICENSING.md maps every feature and
the key files to its licence. Get an Enterprise licence: https://runback.dev/contact
